pr"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 372002, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Ugq4pAmp15maCQyS8pXjs4", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_malformed"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-pr", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 372002, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Ugq4pAmp15maCQyS8pXjs4", "kind": "garbled", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 373741, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The nightly failure is fixed and PR #101 is open against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Its docstring and `tests/test_money.py` call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (FIN-212), so `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, I changed the import and the `quantize` call to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101), base `main`, reviewer `alex`.\n\nI did not merge. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so that step is still pending.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LGYuheRSdyxpmmX4cF1WWg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VoZg6Azzb3hiW9iskXka7q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CAyN4oxByQJYKupktryfHB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and the test both call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Under half-up, `2.665` becomes `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`. I'll create a branch and make the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KNGcaQ8hbi5eGmVKtVDLVE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Lndc3ak4UNUUMSkHoMaxNJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The commit is on the branch. Next I'll start CI against it and wait for the result.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Mnz9dwoCZT6LmVd7shT45v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019JBX4xTzZUWjWMxEUrespg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Ugq4pAmp15maCQyS8pXjs4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and `tests/test_money.py` require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. This caused the nightly build failure.\n\n## Change\n- Import `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` instead of `ROUND_HALF_UP`\n- Use it in `quantize`\n\n## Verification\n- CI run `ci-0001` passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- `test_half_even` checks `2.675 -> 2.68` and `2.665 -> 2.66`, which match half-even rounding.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-pr"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed and PR #101 is open against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Its docstring and `tests/test_money.py` call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (FIN-212), so `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, I changed the import and the `quantize` call to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101), base `main`, reviewer `alex`.\n\nI did not merge. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so that step is still pending.", "type": "text"}]}]}